# Feature folder layout

Full guide: `docs/agents/feature-layout.md` (ADR-0003).

## Shape

```text
src/features/<name>/
  commands/ | listeners/ | interaction-handlers/   # Sapphire pieces only
  lib/
    attach-<name>.ts | container-augment.ts        # wiring / DI typing
    <domain>/                                      # one folder per concern
    <tiny-helper>.ts                               # only until it earns a folder
```

Music domains today: `lib/session/`, `lib/music-node/`, `lib/control-surface/`.

## Do

- Split `lib/` by **domain concern** (session, music-node, control-surface), not by layer
- Colocate `*.test.ts` and port+fake with the module they belong to
- Keep commands/handlers thin; import from `lib/<domain>/`
- Name folders with CONTEXT.md vocabulary
- Put durable tables in `lib/<domain>/schema.ts` (Drizzle Kit globs `src/features/**/schema.ts`)

## Don't

- Dump new modules into a flat `lib/` once a domain folder already exists for that concern
- Nest Sapphire piece folders under `lib/`
- Put Kazagumo/Discord clients in core (`src/lib/`) — feature `lib/` only
- Create `adapters/` / `domain/` / `ui/` trees unless a concern truly needs them
- Put Drizzle table schemas outside `src/features/` or edit `drizzle.config.ts` per feature
